# TASK-260715-1ozsb6 results — review round 4 rework

## Outcome

The pinned libssh2/OpenSSL adapter remains integrated behind the candidate-neutral SSH boundary for the extension-safe macOS provider and harness. This rework closes every blocking finding in `TASK-260715-1ozsb6_review-results-04.md`.

## Review findings closed

1. Long-lived reads no longer use `writeCreditWait`; they remain pending until bytes, EOF, channel disposition, or caller cancellation. Socket completion waiters make cancellation operation-scoped without discarding owned bridge work.
2. External signer completion is independently cancellable. Authentication timeout explicitly cancels and joins the signer before teardown returns resources to baseline.
3. Rekey uses the earlier of the caller-visible explicit deadline and `SSHRekeyPolicy.timeout` before session-gate admission. One keepalive may defer behind an active KEX and automatic keepalive scheduling continues afterward.
4. `finishWriting` queues behind accepted writes on the per-channel FIFO gate. Uncertain EOF and exec/upload failures reset only their channel through fresh cancellation-shielded cleanup. Channel-open rejection is operation-scoped with explicit `unsupported` RFC reason evidence; connection errors remain lane-fatal.

## Conformance evidence

- Idle-read fake-clock advancement proves no implicit timeout; cancellation remains channel-scoped.
- A suspended signer exceeds a 100 ms authentication deadline, is canceled/joined, and leaves all owned resources at zero.
- A rekey queued behind a held channel-open gate expires under `SSHRekeyPolicy.timeout`; keepalive queued behind successful KEX transmits afterward.
- Concurrent same-channel writes plus EOF preserve every accepted byte exactly once and in gate order.
- Exec-exit and upload timeouts reset their exec channels; later sibling exec channels succeed. A rejected direct-tcpip open reports operation scope and preserves an existing direct sibling.
- Consumer-driven receive credit, RFC open-reason taxonomy, exact exec-exit presence/coreDumped, and deep rekey/keepalive observability remain explicit `unsupported` states owned by `TASK-260728-3cveay`.

